{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27276138","formula":"C₂₃H₂₄O₆","hill":"C23H24O6","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":24.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Dimethylcurcumin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dimethylcurcumin (development code ASC-J9) is a nonsteroidal antiandrogen and a synthetic curcuminoid. In vitro, it is an androgen receptor (AR) inhibitor and shows antiandrogenic activity, although its mechanism of action and effects differ from those of conventional antiandrogens; it is not an antagonist of the AR and instead appears to act as a selective degradation enhancer of certain subpopulations of the AR, for instance those present in the prostate gland."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":9952605,"mass":396.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C=C(C=C1)/C=C/C(=O)CC(=O)/C=C/C2=CC(=C(C=C2)OC)OC)OC","inchikey":"HMJSBVCDPKODEX-NXZHAISVSA-N","iupac":"(1E,6E)-1,7-bis(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)hepta-1,6-diene-3,5-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9952605","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":6.931,"y":2.455,"z":0.288,"el":"O"},{"x":-8.417,"y":-1.143,"z":0.084,"el":"O"},{"x":9.014,"y":0.616,"z":0.324,"el":"O"},{"x":-8.652,"y":1.598,"z":-0.309,"el":"O"},{"x":1.126,"y":-2.062,"z":-1.054,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.085,"y":-1.941,"z":0.918,"el":"O"},{"x":5.117,"y":-0.658,"z":-0.328,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.914,"y":-0.114,"z":0.268,"el":"C"},{"x":5.379,"y":0.697,"z":-0.126,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.053,"y":-0.919,"z":0.272,"el":"C"},{"x":6.687,"y":1.129,"z":0.093,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.311,"y":-0.347,"z":0.079,"el":"C"},{"x":7.733,"y":0.206,"z":0.11,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.429,"y":1.028,"z":-0.12,"el":"C"},{"x":6.163,"y":-1.581,"z":-0.312,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.032,"y":1.262,"z":0.069,"el":"C"},{"x":0.114,"y":-0.104,"z":-0.079,"el":"C"},{"x":3.735,"y":-1.115,"z":-0.559,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.585,"y":-0.717,"z":0